Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 05:17:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] generalized-bulletproofs: test verify_split against
 verify at its chunk boundaries

verify_split clamps `parts` to terms.len() / 1024 (at least 1) and cuts the
term list into chunks of ceil(len / parts) terms. The new tests build batch
verifiers with an exact number of multiexp terms around every edge of that
arithmetic (3, 1023-1025, 2047-2049, 3072-3073, 4097, 12288-12289, 24575,
24581 terms) and check, for parts 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 12, 24 and 1000, that
verify_split accepts a batch whose multiexp sums to the identity, and
rejects the same batch with one scalar changed. The changed term is placed
at the start, at the end and on both sides of every chunk boundary, so a
chunk that is dropped, repeated or cut wrongly changes a verdict. Every
changed batch is also checked against verify. A second test pins the
clamp's edges.

Result: 14 lengths, 8 parts settings, 942 changed batches, all rejected by
both; every identity batch accepted; the whole generalized-bulletproofs
suite passes (rustc 1.99.1, --features tests).

Asked for by the second reviewer (item 3a of its monerodato.1 review).
Test-only: the module is #[cfg(test)].

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
